{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "yaaw.review/v2",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema",
    "ticket",
    "round",
    "result",
    "ticket_revision",
    "spec_revision",
    "repository",
    "evidence"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "schema": {
      "const": "yaaw.review/v2"
    },
    "ticket": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^TASK-[0-9]+$"
    },
    "round": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 1
    },
    "result": {
      "enum": [
        "PASS",
        "REPAIR",
        "REPLAN",
        "BLOCKED"
      ]
    },
    "ticket_revision": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0
    },
    "spec_revision": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0
    },
    "repository": {
      "$ref": "repository-identity.schema.json"
    },
    "evidence": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "affected_paths": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1
      },
      "uniqueItems": true
    },
    "scope_verified": {
      "type": "boolean"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}

## Canonical ticket-scoped proof on every PASS verification
When verifying a ticket with nonempty, safe `affected_paths`, run:
`node .yaaw-core/system/engine/scope-identity.mjs --workspace <WORKSPACE_ROOT> --ticket TASK-NNN`
after all verification checks and after capturing exact canonical repository identity. If the tool returns READY, include its JSON verbatim in new immutable `yaaw.evidence/v3` verification under `scope_identity`. If UNKNOWN, do **not** invent or reconstruct a scope digest; report the missing scope/error and leave the verified application and original evidence unchanged. Scope identity is additional assurance, not a substitute for the full repository identity and ticket/spec revisions. Reviewer must independently recompute the same scope and confirm that it sufficiently covers implemented application code and shared interfaces.
